19770                       / ADJACENT RULERS (WHICH MAY BE DELETED IN THE PROCESS).
19771                       /
19772                       / WE WILL CONCATENATE ADJACENT RULERS BY MOVING THE CURSOR
19773                       / BACK THEN FORWARD OVER THEM.  WHEN WE DO THIS,
19774                       / WE WILL FORGET THE CURRENT CURSOR LOCATION WITHIN
19775                       / THE LINE, SINCE THERE IS A TINY CHANCE THAT THERE
19776                       / ARE 50 OR MORE ADJACENT RULERS, AND THAT MOVING
19777                       / OVER THEM WILL CAUSE DATA TO BE SCROLLED IN FROM
19778                       / DISK OVER THE PLACE IN THE EDIT BUFFER CORRESPSN$.
19779                       /
19780                       / WE WILL CONCATRSOR LOCATION!
19781                       / PARANOID, ISN'T IT?
19782                       /
19783                       / AT ANY RATE, THE CURSOR WILL BE LEFT AT THE
19784                       / BEGINNING OF THE LINE.
