24677               /       PUTSTP  WRITE TO PASTE BUFFER
24678               /
24679               /       THIS ROUTINE TAKES CHARACTERS PASSED IN THE AC AND PUTS THEM IN
24680               /       THE PASTE DISK BUFFER.  WHEN THE BUFFER IS FULL IT WRITES THE
24681               /       BUFFER TO DISK.  WHEN THE LAST ALLOCATED DISK BLOCK IS WRITTEN
24682               /       IT SETS THE CUT OVERFLOW FLAG AND TAKES A SKIP RETURN.
24683               /
24684               /       CALL:
24685               /
24686               /       JMS     PUTSTP  (AC := CHARACTER TO WRITEOUT)
24687               /       (RETURNS HERE IF OK)
24688               /       (RETURNS HERE ON END OF PASTE BUFFER)
24689               /       
24690               /       RETURNS WITH AC:=0 IN ALL CASES
24691               /
24692               PUTSTP, XX                      /ENTRY POINT
full                 ^
undefined              	 ^
     057307* 0000  
24693                       CDFBUF                  /SET TO BUFFER FIELD
undefined       	     ^
     057310* 0000  
